## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates the ability to design privacy-preserving cross-region data flows with governance, compliance, and zero-trust architectural principles.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region secure multi-party computation (MPC) with differential privacy
- Per-tenant policy management without service interruption
- Immutable audit trails with cryptographic hashing
- Key rotation and hot configuration deployment

## Code Example

```javascript
// API surface definition
const apiSpecification = [
  { 
    path: '/cca_score/share', 
    method: 'POST', 
    body: ['tenant_id', 'region', 'encrypted_share', 'model_version'],
    response: { status: 'accepted', share_id: 'uuid' }
  },
  { 
    path: '/cca_score/aggregate', 
    method: 'POST', 
    body: ['aggregation_id', 'regions'],
    response: { status: 'completed', result: 'encrypted_aggregate' }
  },
  { 
    path: '/cca_score/config', 
    method: 'GET', 
    query: ['tenant_id'],
    response: { retention_days: 90, governance_rules: [] }
  }
];

// Data model
interface CCAScoreConfig {
  tenant_id: string;
  region: string;
  model_version: string;
  retention_days: number;
  audit_hash: string;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests system design for real-time collaboration at scale, including choice of transport, state partitioning, conflict resolution, and delivery guarantees.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time collaboration data models (CRDTs vs OT)
- Transport choices (WebSocket vs gRPC)
- Per-room sharding and snapshotting
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple CRDT merge sketch
class ORSet {
  constructor() { this.add = new Set(); this.remove = new Set(); }
  apply(op) { if (op.type === 'add') this.add.add(op.id); else if (op.type === 'remove') this.remove.add(op.id); }
  value() { return [...this.add].filter(id => !this.remove.has(id)); }
  merge(other) { this.add = new Set([...this.add, ...other.add]); this.remove = new Set([...this.remove, ...other.remove]); }
}
```

